-- title:
--   Finite fields of characteristic p embed into A/pA for A⊆ℂ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime number and let $k$ be a finite field of characteristic $p$ (so $k$ is a field, finite, and of characteristic $p$ in the sense of `CharP`). The assertion is that there exists a subring $A$ of $\mathbb{C}$ such that the ideal of $A$ generated by the single element $p$ (the image of the natural number $p$ under the canonical map $\mathbb{N}\to A$) is a maximal ideal of $A$, together with a ring homomorphism from $k$ to the quotient $A/pA$; the existence of the homomorphism is expressed as the nonemptiness of the type $k \to_{+*} A/pA$. No minimality or finiteness condition is imposed on $A$, and no injectivity is asserted for the homomorphism, although it is automatically injective since $k$ is a field and $A/pA$ is nonzero, $pA$ being maximal. Note that the existence of the maximality witness and of the homomorphism is packaged as a single nested existential statement over $A$.
--
--   This is the monogenic case of the Dedekind–Kummer theorem read in the direction of realisation: every finite field of characteristic $p$ arises as a residue field $A/pA$ with $p$ inert in an order $A=\mathbb{Z}[\alpha]\subseteq\mathbb{C}$. It is used to realise a finite residue field inside a quotient of a subring of $\mathbb{C}$, in the construction of semilinear maps on the two-dimensional eigenspace attached to the Tate module of a modular curve in the ordinary case.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FiniteField_exists_subring_complex_isMaximal_span_natCast_ringHom.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
